leaf INFO (level inherited from mid): [leaf, top1, top2]
leaf FINE (parents' levels are not consulted): [leaf, top1, top2]
leaf WARNING: [leaf, mid, top1, top2]
leaf FINER hidden: []
mid WARNING: [mid, top1, top2]
top WARNING (its own level SEVERE hides it): []
top SEVERE: [top1, top2]
mid stops the walk: [leaf, mid]
leaf stops the walk: [leaf]
leaf filter refuses: nothing: []
a parent's filter does not gate a child's record: [leaf, mid, top1, top2]
mid filter gates its own: []
the logger calls handlers whatever their level: [blind-, blind2-]
filter then handler: [filter:fl2.named:yes, handler:fl2.named:yes, filter:fl2.named:no]
handlers: child first, then parent: [child, parent saw fl2.p.c]
handler exception: [thrower, caught from handler]
shared handler: [shared, shared]
handler levels: [warn, all, fine, all, fine, all, fine, all, warn, all, fine]
